{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>בא גד.</b> A good fortune has come, like ״גַּד גַּדִּי וְסָנוּק לָא״ (Shabbat 67), and similar to it ״הָעֹרְכִים לַגַּד שֻׁלְחָן״ (Isaiah 65). And from an aggadic viewpoint — that he was born circumcised, like ״גֹּדוּ אִילָנָא״ (Daniel 4). And I do not know why תֵּבָה אַחַת ['one word'] was written. Another interpretation: why is the single word called בָּגָד? Like ״בָּגַדְתָּ בִּי״ — when you came to my maidservant, like a man who betrays the wife of his youth."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "תיבה אחת ('one word') refers to the single-word utterance 'בא גד'; Rashi then plays on the word בגד meaning both 'betray' and the letters ב-ג-ד as a unit."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:15.953178010Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}